  "title": "Nakanishi2015 – SSVEP Nakanishi 2015 dataset",
  "description": "This dataset comprises 12-class steady-state visual evoked potential (SSVEP) recordings acquired from 10 healthy subjects using 8 EEG channels during a brain-computer interface task. The study compared canonical correlation analysis (CCA)-based methods for SSVEP detection. Data were preprocessed with bandpass filtering (6-80 Hz) and downsampled to 256 Hz, with 180 trials per subject organized in 15 blocks of 12 trials each.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were acquired using a Biosemi ActiveTwo amplifier with 8 electrodes (PO7, PO3, POz, PO4, PO8, O1, Oz, O2) positioned according to the standard 10-20 montage with CMS/DRL reference. Sampling rate was 256 Hz. Subjects performed a 12-class SSVEP target identification task with joint frequency-phase modulation (9.25-14.75 Hz range, 0.5 Hz resolution). Each trial consisted of a 1-second cue period followed by 4 seconds of flickering visual stimuli presented on a 4×3 matrix at 60 Hz refresh rate. Preprocessing included zero-phase IIR bandpass filtering (6-80 Hz) and epoch extraction with 135-ms latency compensation for visual system delay.",
